 scheduler, reflection, eval, host IO and hosted-profile leakage; unsupported dynamic forms reject unless eliminated with evidence. Dependencies: Lower supplies target ABI/artifacts, Legality supplies profile facts, and Build supplies package policy; no product ISA or platform choice is made here.\n\n- [ ] `runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/finish-managednative-execution-startup-panic-and-cleanup` Finish managed/native execution, startup, panic and cleanup\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Development evaluator](../../bootstrap/gravity/src/gravity/runtime.gravity) and [native manifest](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/foundation/00287-minimal-native-runtime-manifest.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Executed startup/failure/resource fixtures and manifest-to-service agreement; before user code, validate selected provider existence, artifact versions, grant scopes, compiled contracts, profile/target compatibility and enabled safety/audit requirements; reject a missing required provider unless a declared fallback applies, with positive fallback and negative mismatch fixtures under [L15 runtime providers](../../docs/phase-01-core-language/025-l15-capability-provider-specification.md) . R1/R3/R4: typed host adapters with effects, capabilities, taint, error and source-map contracts; selected host/version/module/collection/dynamic-state manifests; startup, initialization, handoff and teardown order; explicit panic/trap/abort/unwind/result policy; host null/undefined conversion, exception and rejected-promise translation; Gravity equality/hashing/serialization conformance; deterministic linear cleanup independent of process exit or GC. Reject undeclared helper effects, untranslated/null foreign values and GC-only linear cleanup; debug services must be absent or release-policy marked. Dependencies: Lower supplies ABI and source maps, Legality supplies legal services, and Auth supplies grants; selected compiler services do not close all managed/native targets. P4: execute deterministic cleanup for linear host resources despite GC; managed objects remain GC-managed and only an explicit boundary can rely on finalizer timing. Reject GC-only cleanup where deterministic release is required; preserve exactly-once flow evidence from Legality separately from executed terminal operations. Translate host errors through the declared Gravity failure channel with source/generated origins.\n\n- [ ] `runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries` Implement memory, concurrency and typed FFI boundaries\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Runtime contracts](../../docs/phase-08-runtime-architecture/README.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Allocation, lifetime, transfer, race and foreign-failure conformance with explicit providers. Execute the [SAFE2-SAFE8 contracts](../../docs/phase-02-safety/README.md): declared allocation and cleanup failures, partial initialization cleanup, region/arena generation and borrow checks, release through the correct allocator/provider, callback lifetime/thread/reentrancy/release and foreign error/exception/promise translation. Reject retained borrows, post-reset access, missing FFI declarations, unsupported atomics and unsynchronized mutable access; validate immutable sharing, lock cleanup, actor/channel transfer and declared backpressure/cancellation. Inspect actual checks and audit records, with no hidden GC or host-thread fallback. . R3/R5/R6/R10: allocation/deallocation/provider manifests, no-allocation and region/arena escape rejection, linear acquire/transfer/consume ledgers, device address-space/transfer/synchronization/lifetime checks, audited raw-memory wrappers, and agreement of retained checks with exact proof-elision records; atomics with target memory order/scope/alignment, structured task parent or explicit lifecycle owner, cancellation cleanup and failure propagation, actor/channel schemas with ordering/backpressure/transfer policy; FFI symbol/loading policy, ABI/layout conformance, null/handle/lifetime/ownership/error adapters and callbacks re-entering capability/taint/thread-affinity/scheduler checks. Reject mismatched providers, races, orphan tasks, unsupported atomics, schemaless messages, raw extern safe calls and invalid callback entry. Dependencies: ownership and Legality supply compile-time facts, Lower supplies target layouts, Auth supplies grants, and distributed execution supplies replay policy; runtime debug checks cannot substitute for compile-time safety. P4/P5: host-object/native FFI records bind runtime/version/symbol, Gravity and foreign types, rooting/ownership/lifetime, nullability, failure mapping, affinity, ABI, effects/grants and safe wrappers. Insufficient host metadata permits opaque provider-only handles, not unrestricted manipulation; raw native imports are not directly safe-callable. Exercise positive boundaries and missing metadata, ungranted call, invalid lifetime and untranslated failure rejection.\n\n- [ ] `runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-distributedai-replay-and-interactive-execution` Connect distributed/AI replay and interactive execution\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Runtime contracts](../../docs/phase-08-runtime-architecture/README.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Recorded nondeterminism, replay equality, no undeclared duplicated external effect, REPL grant denial. R6/R7/R8/R9: topology/provider/event-log/state/message schemas; durable idempotency, timeout/retry/cancellation/failure/compensation records; migration or rejection of replay-incompatible code/topology/schema changes; model/provider/prompt provenance, output and sink validation, policy-recorded provider substitution, typed tool contracts with caller/callee grants and policy-required human review, memory/retrieval privacy/retention/deletion/taint controls and secret redaction; R7/R8 replay-required segments return recorded model/tool/retrieval/memory/review decisions or reject a missing record. R