fig loaders record deterministic source precedence, defaults/required\nfields, environment identity, secret access/rotation/audit and redaction policy.\nReads require declared effects and grants; external inputs stay tainted until\nvalidated. Hermetic builds capture config inputs or reject the reads. Reload\nfixtures require compatibility, lifecycle and observability policy. Reject\nambient reads, missing validation and secrets in logs, manifests, source maps,\nprompts, traces or diagnostics except policy-allowed redacted markers.\n\nS9: validators cover each declared artifact kind and the common versioned\nsource/compiler/dependency/pass provenance, profile/target/backend/runtime,\neffects/grants, content identity, safety/proof/diagnostic/conformance envelope.\nPreserve relevant unsafe-island, AI/tool, generated-code and redaction records;\nrequire canonical hash/signing/replay/release inputs, bootstrap provenance for\ngraph cycles, and compatibility/migration records for version changes. Missing\nrequired release evidence rejects at the schema gate; Release owns the actual\nrelease decision. Each S1-S9 fixture records its stable diagnostic family,\nschema/artifact identity, failing path or edge, applicable source/target/boundary\nand remediation. These clauses specify future evidence, not passing results.\n\n", :after-sha256 "7201572d14ff5260ae4097b9d16a0d945761b0977aea137421a777dc135a7eee"} {:path "specs/legality-workflow/tasks.md", :requirements ["gravity/profile-contract-declaration"], :before-sha256 "a222dc3cd10cd6d7e95e9f7ebcf4a64beb079ac6e2ce3a2663f987e9b12a57fb", :marker "legality-implementation-tasks", :operation :replace-exact-task-record, :status-change :none, :after "- [ ] `legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks` Complete profile restrictions and generated-form checks\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Profile contract](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/profile_validation/contract.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Allowed profile matrix and hidden-allocation/reflection/effect rejection before lowering. For SAFE1/SAFE2/SAFE4, reject unavailable checks, memory regimes and provider metadata before backend lowering; distinguish safe, safe-optimized, audited-unsafe, systems, trusted-runtime, experimental and unsafe claims, including weaker dependency modes. Prove or check actual lifetime, layout and failure conditions; no project work allowance substitutes for those semantics. P1/P2/P3/P4/P5/P12: validate one active profile (retaining the explicit implementation-seed exception), reusable support sets/exclusions, and post-expansion/pre-optimization admission; emit portable manifests with dependencies/target/providers. Reject hidden runtime services, impure core generation, unsupported facets and generated-profile violations. Core values remain independent of concrete allocation identity; meta raw memory/FFI requires an explicitly allowed audited implementation-provider boundary. Formal admission rejects unmodeled effects/nondeterminism/unsafe code; assumptions remain explicit. Effect allowances and capability grants are separate checks with an explicit provider mapping, never an intersection of differently typed labels. Foundation requirement gravity/profile-contract-declaration: Publish each claimed profile's permitted, rejected, checked and delegated behavior with backend/runtime/provider dependencies and required evidence; enforce the profile contract after expansion and before affected lowering. Refusals: Reject implicit hosted services, hidden effects or allocation, unavailable checks and a claimed profile relying solely on target/runtime refusal; effects and capability grants remain separately typed contracts. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence; pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products.\n\n", :id "legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks", :before "- [ ] `legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks` Complete profile restrictions and generated-form checks\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Profile contract](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/profile_validation/contract.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Allowed profile matrix and hidden-allocation/reflection/effect rejection before lowering. For SAFE1/SAFE2/SAFE4, reject unavailable checks, memory regimes and provider metadata before backend lowering; distinguish safe, safe-optimized, audited-unsafe, systems, trusted-runtime, experimental and unsafe claims, including weaker dependency modes. Prove or check actual lifetime, layout and failure conditions; no project work allowance substitutes for those semantics. P1/P2/P3/P4/P5/P12: validate one active profile (retaining the explicit implementation-seed exception), reusable support sets/exclusions, and post-expansion/pre-optimization admission; emit portable manifests with dependencies/target/providers. Reject hidden runtime services, impure core generation, unsupported facets and generated-profile violations. Core values remain independent of concrete allocation identity; meta raw memory/FFI requires an explicitly allowed audited implementation-provider boundary. Formal admission rejects unmodeled effects/nondeterminism/unsafe code; assumptions remain explicit. Effect allowances and capability grants are separate checks with an explicit provider mapping, never an intersection of differently typed labels.\n\n", :after-sha256 "b44e1e80fcfb698d9126a451303d8b954fbb0ac4eaa6c1392478822ba0f8a3f7"} {:path "specs/legality-workflow/tasks.md", :requirements ["gravity/safety-family-conformance" "gravity/unsafe-island-safe-api-eligibility"], :before-sha256 "1c56fef6af3af4320bc4ad7dd5a167e9f8ede097209fa65876d157378eb9647b", :marker "legality-implementation-tasks", :operation :replace-exact-task-record, :status-change :none, :after "- [ ] `legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries` Complete safe-code classification and taint/unsafe boundaries\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Safety contract](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/c10_safety_analysis/contract.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Every dangerous operation classified and unclassified operations rejected. Under the [SAFE1/SAFE6-SAFE11/SAFE15 contracts](plan.md), inspect real checks before operations with defined profile-legal failure, complete unsafe audits even when permitted, wrapper preconditions and cleanup, source-bound review invalidation and dependency policy. Reject incomplete FFI contracts, unsupported atomics, implicit narrowing, undeclared relaxed numerics, taint loss, incompatible sanitizers and unvalidated deserialization; preserve residual taint and secret redaction. Emit inspectable outcome, proof, trust and audit records; internal-only unsafe boundaries confer no safe public API. Explicit wrapping/saturating conversions retain their unresolved relation to checked/proven narrowing. Runtime/provider execution and domain-specific consumers require their own evidence. P12: proof consumers check theorem/source/certificate/hash-chain/trusted-kernel/assumption/profile/target agreement; unverified imports are ignored or rejected only as policy states. Proof production and symbolic lowering are separate Math producer interfaces; a profile check alone cannot close them. Foundation requirement gravity/safety-family-conformance: Exercise each claimed safety family on accepted safe programs, rejected illegal programs and explicit audited unsafe-island cases; retain the applicable proven-safe, runtime-checked, rejected or unsafe-island outcome, owning diagnostics and evidence. Refusals: Reject an unclassified dangerous operation, hidden unsafe path, stale proof/audit or missing actual runtime-check failure case; no fifth implicit outcome or undefined safe behavior is allowed. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/unsafe-island-safe-api-eligibility: Expose unsafe-backed functionality as a safe API only when the wrapper proves or checks every required precondition and cleanup obligation, with source-bound audit and actual boundary tests; preserve internal-only status as a separate permitted boundary. Refusals: Reject invalid state escaping into safe code, a missing wrapper test/audit, an unproved precondition or treating internal-only unsafe code as a safe exported API. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products.\n\n", :id "legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries", :before "- [ ] `legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries` Complete safe-code classification and taint/unsafe boundaries\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Safety contract](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/c10_safety_analysis/contract.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Every dangerous operation classified and unclassified operations rejected. Under the [SAFE1/SAFE6-SAFE11/SAFE15 contracts](plan.md), inspect real checks before operations with defined profile-legal failure, complete unsafe audits even when permitted, wrapper preconditions and cleanup, source-bound review invalidation and dependency policy. Reject incomplete FFI contracts, unsupported atomics, implicit narrowing, undeclared relaxed numerics, taint loss, incompatible sanitizers and unvalidated deserialization; preserve residual taint and secret redaction. Emit inspectable outcome, proof, trust and audit records; internal-only unsafe boundaries confer no safe public API. Explicit wrapping/saturating conversions retain their unresolved relation to checked/proven narrowing. Runtime/provider execution and domain-specific consumers require their own evidence. P12: proof consumers check theorem/source/certificate/hash-chain/trusted-kernel/assumption/profile/target agreement; unverified imports are ignored or rejected only as policy states. Proof production and symbolic lowering are separate Math producer interfaces; a profile check alone cannot close them.\n\n", :after-sha256 "ea84988fde248f91d3c6b9b8c5195a6d806850fab4b873ca3f1a72bdfdf9b03c"} {:path "specs/lower-workflow/tasks.md", :requirements ["gravity/multiversion-guard-manifest" "gravity/target-lowering-operation-contract"], :before-sha256 "81caa35a780855ffa1af2171b16d3a2b6b6835049c5ae449adff33e97fe303ee", :marker "lower-implementation-tasks", :operation :replace-exact-task-record, :status-change :none, :after "- [ ] `lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs` lower/1: Validate lowering inputs\n\nCurrent evidence/status: Open; partial source evidence above is not closure\n\nDone when (yes/no): Reject unverified/stale IR and incompatible profiles/features; expose explicit supported-operation and target matrices. P5: admit SIMD/intrinsics only with declared target features, numeric mode and alignment/layout evidence plus a valid fallback or rejection. A target wrapper does not justify unchecked intrinsics or change source legality; guarded variant selection and target lowering remain distinct interfaces. Foundation requirement gravity/multiversion-guard-manifest: For every dispatched backend variant emit target-feature guards, profile and numeric/safety constraints, fallback/rejection behavior and source-bound benchmark evidence; exercise each variant and guard failure. Refusals: Reject an unguarded unavailable instruction, widened profile, unjustified fast path, absent valid fallback or a benchmark from a different variant/target. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/target-lowering-operation-contract: For every MIR/domain operation in the declared input closure emit its explicit accept/lower/delegate/reject disposition with target, profile, ABI/provider and preservation obligations, and consume that disposition at target emission. Refusals: Reject an uncovered operation, stale/unverified IR, unsupported feature or delegate that widens effects/authority or drops source/safety/proof facts; emit an owning unsupported-operation diagnostic. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products.\n\n", :id "lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs", :before "- [ ] `lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs` lower/1: Validate lowering inputs\n\nCurrent evidence/status: Open; partial source evidence above is not closure\n\nDone when (yes/no): Reject unverified/stale IR and incompatible profiles/features; expose explicit supported-operation and target matrices. P5: admit SIMD/intrinsics only with declared target features, numeric mode and alignment/layout evidence plus a valid fallback or rejection. A target wrapper does not justify unchecked intrinsics or change source legality; guarded variant selection and target lowering remain distinct interfaces.\n\n", :after-sha256 "082f54c1192abfb5b8fc20e6391b50bf94c1bd4db8866b7e141753100a8a3af3"} {:path "specs/lower-workflow/tasks.md", :requirements ["gravity/native-target-artifact-emission"], :before-sha256 "d7bd0f1f0dbe0f340be6b6a94e478f96141ae04880c77c16db14fb5a9afdf2cd", :marker "lower-implementation-tasks", :operation :replace-exact-task-record, :status-change :none, :after "- [ ] `lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower5-integrate-target-emission` lower/5: Integrate target emission\n\nCurrent evidence/status: Open; partial source evidence above is not closure\n\nDone when (yes/no): Feed Emit accepted backend-ready inputs and rejected unsupported-feature cases for the selected staged Linux LLVM release candidate; keep hosted development evidence separate, without claiming every platform. Foundation requirement gravity/native-target-artifact-emission: Emit a real C/LLVM native object or executable for D2's declared typed CLI slice from verified MIR, selected target ABI/runtime/provider records and complete source/compiler/artifact provenance; inspect and execute the claimed output where required by that slice. Refusals: Reject unchecked MIR, an unsupported operation/target, missing runtime/provider evidence and a metadata-only or nonnative output presented as the required native artifact. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs - Verified MIR/domain-operation disposition matrix and target/provider/preservation inputs; runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence; build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix - Locked source/compiler/provider/target build graph and canonical rebuild comparison.\n\n", :id "lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower5-integrate-target-emission", :before "- [ ] `lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower5-integrate-target-emission` lower/5: Integrate target emission\n\nCurrent evidence/status: Open; partial source evidence above is not closure\n\nDone when (yes/no): Feed Emit accepted backend-ready inputs and rejected unsupported-feature cases for the selected staged Linux LLVM release candidate; keep hosted development evidence separate, without claiming every platform.\n\n", :after-sha256 "656b0482677939e7425a7bf53a63ba781b967155d2439fc4064813be86cd5f55"} {:path "specs/platform-workflow/tasks.md", :requirements ["gravity/realtime-not-throughput-proof"], :before-sha256 "c4257dbeaaddb398f9d6b53af9916d7f1db3c4312ddb7cd4b41ffd53033f0aad", :marker "platform-implementation-tasks", :operation :replace-exact-task-record, :status-change :none, :after "- [ ] `firmware` Firmware / `firmware`\n\nStatus: Open\n\nDeclared completion and remaining work: Adopt device memory/startup target; implement interrupt/MMIO/startup and explicit allocation; verify image/link map and rejected unsupported services on execution or named emulator. DOM2 acceptance requires memory map, startup/reset, interrupt vectors, stack/static-allocation/section and panic/BSP records; typed volatile/ordered/capability-checked MMIO and audited wrappers; declared interrupt effects and synchronization. Exercise timer sensor reset/acknowledgement/buffer/panic behavior and UART, reject hidden hosted services and unauthorized MMIO, and emit image/link/source/audit maps with boot/simulator evidence. Dependencies: profile legality, native lowering and runtime memory/startup boundaries; physical memory representability remains separate from removed project accounting ; P6 target conformance requires explicit stack/static/region/arena/provider capacity/reset/failure policy and no hidden GC/host services; unknown stack use rejects in strict mode. Check device-map address/width/alignment/volatility/order/grants, interrupt source/priority/shared-state/atomic/reentrancy/stack/latency/context, and required physical loop/recursion/blocking-timeout evidence; missing evidence rejects or requires the policy-permitted unsafe audit. Reject invalid maps, missing device authority, host calls and unbounded handler behavior. Emit image/linker/memory/device/vector/interrupt/latency/safety manifests with source provenance. Physical memory/timing requirements are not compiler work allowances; product target choice remains unassessed Foundation requirement gravity/realtime-not-throughput-proof: For a realtime claim record the declared deadline and worst-case execution/latency/jitter assumptions, target, interference, allocation/blocking/interrupt policy and applicable analysis or measurement evidence; retain throughput benchmarks as a different evidence class. Refusals: Reject deadline guarantees inferred from mean throughput, a different target/load, missing worst-case assumptions or hidden blocking/allocation; physical timing constraints are not compiler work quotas. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts.\n\nSource basis: [Firmware contract](../../docs/phase-09-domain-specific-computing-coverage/125-dom2-firmware-and-embedded-domain-specification.md)\n\n", :id "firmware", :before "- [ ] `firmware` Firmware / `firmware`\n\nStatus: Open\n\nDeclared completion and remaining work: Adopt device memory/startup target; implement interrupt/MMIO/startup and explicit allocation; verify image/link map and rejected unsupported services on execution or named emulator. DOM2 acceptance requires memory map, startup/reset, interrupt vectors, stack/static-allocation/section and panic/BSP records; typed volatile/ordered/capability-checked MMIO and audited wrappers; declared interrupt effects and synchronization. Exercise timer sensor reset/acknowledgement/buffer/panic behavior and UART, reject hidden hosted services and unauthorized MMIO, and emit image/link/source/audit maps with boot/simulator evidence. Dependencies: profile legality, native lowering and runtime memory/startup boundaries; physical memory representability remains separate from removed project accounting ; P6 target conformance requires explicit stack/static/region/arena/provider capacity/reset/failure policy and no hidden GC/host services; unknown stack use rejects in strict mode. Check device-map address/width/alignment/volatility/order/grants, interrupt source/priority/shared-state/atomic/reentrancy/stack/latency/context, and required physical loop/recursion/blocking-timeout evidence; missing evidence rejects or requires the policy-permitted unsafe audit. Reject invalid maps, missing device authority, host calls and unbounded handler behavior. Emit image/linker/memory/device/vector/interrupt/latency/safety manifests with source provenance. Physical memory/timing requirements are not compiler work allowances; product target choice remains unassessed\n\nSource basis: [Firmware contract](../../docs/phase-09-domain-specific-computing-coverage/125-dom2-firmware-and-embedded-domain-specification.md)\n\n", :after-sha256 "26feb5c26d04904ca4054c0d1c47d339f4c7ae8877385dd6100c595ea543b579"} {:path "specs/release-workflow/tasks.md", :requirements ["gravity/coverage-claim-slice" "gravity/coverage-claim-status-distinction" "gravity/coverage-positive-negative-fixtures" "gravity/documentation-lock-scope" "gravity/foundation-semantic-change-control" "gravity/migration-provenance-safety" "gravity/milestone-contract-sequencing" "gravity/milestone-evidence-bundle" "gravity/milestone-executable-evidence" "gravity/real-domain-coverage-evidence" "gravity/release-matrix-evidence" "gravity/replacement-parity-evidence" "gravity/replacement-slice-record"], :before-sha256 "c869d2588a29f524e87e0d19512d3e75d7e4dcf76417e8e05445b6a9dd72d914", :marker "release-implementation-tasks", :operation :replace-exact-task-record, :status-change :none, :after "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-each-claimed-component-to-exact-implementation-and-conformance` Bind each claimed component to exact implementation and conformance\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Overall roadmap](../../docs/implementation-roadmap.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Component outcome receipts, positive/negative programs and explicit unsupported surface. Maintain the source-bound task/disposition matrix for all 240 original contracts and the separately declared release and Platform Product extensions. Keep every missing producer/checker/consumer interface, alias or split question, and architecture choice as finite named remaining work with criteria, dependencies and accountable role; an accountability link does not establish an implementation interface. Resolve those decisions and bind actual component evidence before claiming the corresponding release scope. This release-claim obligation does not block ordinary semantic development. Foundation requirement gravity/coverage-claim-slice: Publish each domain coverage claim as an exact behavior slice with source forms, profile, target/backend, provider/runtime assumptions, emitted artifacts and explicit unsupported boundaries, linked to the actual demonstrating product. Refusals: Reject a whole-domain claim supported only by a smaller slice, a missing profile/target, or a provider adapter presented as a complete replacement. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products. Foundation requirement gravity/coverage-claim-status-distinction: Classify every declared coverage entry as implemented, designed, delegated, experimental, unsupported or out of scope with its concrete source/evidence basis; expose the classification to consumers of the claim. Refusals: Reject promoting a designed/delegated/example-only entry to implemented, silently dropping unsupported entries or treating absent evidence as out of scope. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Foundation requirement gravity/coverage-positive-negative-fixtures: For each claimed domain slice retain real accepted and rejected input fixtures with expected artifacts and structured owning diagnostics, executed through the claimed implementation/provider boundary. Refusals: Reject coverage evidence missing either accepted execution or the relevant invalid-input refusal; synthetic model agreement and a catalogue name alone cannot close the slice. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/integrate-runtimebuildeditor-consumers-without-rule-drift - Actual runtime/compiler/tool structured diagnostics with stable owning codes and provenance. Foundation requirement gravity/documentation-lock-scope: Assess the explicit D2 M0 forty-document documentation lock against each of its five named exit gates, retaining the exact document set, source hashes, reviewed results and unresolved gate failures; label the decision documentation-only. Refusals: Reject a lock missing any named document or gate, stale source evidence, or an attempt to turn that documentation decision into executable compiler, milestone or release acceptance. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Foundation requirement gravity/foundation-semantic-change-control: For a changed foundation guarantee publish the affected D0-D9 and downstream contract set, compatibility decision, changed conformance fixtures and evidence invalidations before claiming the changed support. Refusals: Reject a semantic change without affected-contract review, stale acceptance reuse or omitted compatibility/fixture updates; the policy record is not actual approval of the change. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): tools/finite-service-outcomes-and-remaining-work/lint-analysis-tool-maintainer - Canonical D3 vocabulary/layer maps and source/manifest terminology check results; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/migration-provenance-safety: For a generated/migrated replacement slice preserve incumbent/source/generator provenance, recheck generated code and unsafe audit boundaries, and record the scoped conformance and performance evidence needed before retiring its interop path. Refusals: Reject interop retirement on translation success alone, missing provenance/audits or unexplained behavioral/performance differences; preserve policy-qualified narrowed and unsupported cases. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries - Dangerous-operation outcomes, actual checks, proof references and audited wrapper boundaries; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/milestone-contract-sequencing: Bind each milestone claim to its governing upstream contracts and actual declared interface products in D2 order; record early downstream work as a supported interface experiment with explicit non-release scope. Refusals: Reject downstream support claims without required upstream contracts or evidence; do not block ordinary isolated development merely because a different component is incomplete. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products. Foundation requirement gravity/milestone-evidence-bundle: Assemble the D2 milestone bundle for the exact claimed surface: governing document versions, real accepted/rejected programs, diagnostics, emitted artifacts, profile/target matrices, safety/trust boundaries, reproducibility and open risks. Refusals: Reject a bundle with an omitted required member, stale input identity, unsupported matrix cell or concealed open risk; a document inventory is not an executable bundle. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix - Locked source/compiler/provider/target build graph and canonical rebuild comparison; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/milestone-executable-evidence: Before marking a milestone complete execute its required positive and negative programs through the claimed compiler/runtime path and bind real emitted products and owning diagnostics to the milestone decision. Refusals: Reject milestone completion supported only by plans, schemas, mocked execution, a passing unrelated helper or missing rejection evidence. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-checkruncompilebuildtestpackageverify-to-real-services - Actual source-to-public-command execution, declared stdout authority and outputs; lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower5-integrate-target-emission - Actual target emission artifacts and unsupported-feature diagnostics. Foundation requirement gravity/real-domain-coverage-evidence: Demonstrate the declared domain's actual constraints, integration boundary and produced artifact on a representative real workload, with required rejection cases and an explicit supported subset. Refusals: Reject replacing the required domain behavior with a toy simulation, mock provider, catalogue entry or unrelated subset; simulator evidence is allowed only where the owning contract permits that specific substitute. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/release-matrix-evidence: Bind each milestone/release claim to a versioned profile-by-target/backend/runtime matrix whose claimed cells each link exact accepted/rejected executable evidence and unsupported cells remain explicit. Refusals: Reject a cell supported by another profile/target's receipt, stale compiler/provider inputs or a missing required negative fixture; one cell cannot imply whole-matrix support. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix - Locked source/compiler/provider/target build graph and canonical rebuild comparison; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products. Foundation requirement gravity/replacement-parity-evidence: Before upgrading a named interop slice to replacement status compare actual incumbent and Gravity behavior, diagnostics, effects/capabilities, artifacts and applicable performance on the declared workload, with reviewed deltas and limits. Refusals: Reject replacement promotion from a shim, translation result or toy fixture alone, unexplained divergence or performance evidence from another scope. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix - Locked source/compiler/provider/target build graph and canonical rebuild comparison; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/replacement-slice-record: Publish a versioned replacement-slice record identifying incumbent behavior, actual Gravity source and explicitly preserved, narrowed, delegated and unsupported operations with profile/target/provider and migration provenance. Refusals: Reject a replacement claim omitting a known narrowed/unsupported behavior, silently treating a delegated operation as native replacement or losing the incumbent comparison basis. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products.\n\n", :id "release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-each-claimed-component-to-exact-implementation-and-conformance", :before "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-each-claimed-component-to-exact-implementation-and-conformance` Bind each claimed component to exact implementation and conformance\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Overall roadmap](../../docs/implementation-roadmap.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Component outcome receipts, positive/negative programs and explicit unsupported surface. Maintain the source-bound task/disposition matrix for all 240 original contracts and the separately declared release and Platform Product extensions. Keep every missing producer/checker/consumer interface, alias or split question, and architecture choice as finite named remaining work with criteria, dependencies and accountable role; an accountability link does not establish an implementation interface. Resolve those decisions and bind actual component evidence before claiming the corresponding release scope. This release-claim obligation does not block ordinary semantic development.\n\n", :after-sha256 "4d40470f94eb4c0874e38a908e92947149b6de75a0ceb5f5ba5047fc47f40210"} {:path "specs/release-workflow/tasks.md", :requirements ["gravity/bootstrap-equivalence-before-retirement" "gravity/bootstrap-staged-trust-reduction"], :before-sha256 "6d89f64625816e75bd40e1bcefb8ad13a8befc4bb26de167630bf8dc0a0f87cd", :marker "release-implementation-tasks", :operation :replace-exact-task-record, :status-change :none, :after "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-stage-compatibilityequivalence-across-the-claimed-compiler` Complete stage compatibility/equivalence across the claimed compiler\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Equivalence contract](../../docs/phase-15-bootstrap-and-self-hosting/209-boot7-self-hosting-validation-and-equivalence-plan.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Fresh stage-to-stage outputs and diagnostics, residual trusted-code inventory BOOT1/BOOT3/BOOT5/BOOT7: Publish a versioned row for every claimed stage and authoritative module revision, naming source/compiler/artifact identities, supported and unsupported documents/features/profiles/backends/runtime/package/library/test closure, owned or deferred gaps, conformance links and release eligibility. Record exact compiler-module ownership and residual TCB with measurable migration delta. Compare both named compilers and canonical artifacts under declared applicable hash/manifest/diagnostic/conformance/runtime/IR/performance/accepted-delta modes; preserve stable codes/spans and provenance. Reject missing outputs, implicit inherited support, omitted stage rows, unsupported claims, stale matrix versions and unexplained drift; accept deltas only with policy-linked review. Performance bounds apply only when performance is part of acceptance; no compiler work quota is introduced. Execute the intermediate authoritative stage/module admission decision against this exact candidate and declared subset, consuming the fresh conformance, equivalence/accepted-delta, matrix, provenance, TCB and applicable audit records. Record admit or deny with candidate/source/compiler/artifact identities and failed predicates. Deny failing applicable suites, stale or missing required evidence, unexplained drift, unsupported claimed support and missing ownership/matrix updates. Exercise both a valid intermediate admission and each refusal. Retain explicitly owned/deferred gaps outside the claimed subset; final release policy separately rejects unreviewed gaps for claimed release support. This decision does not produce the evidence it consumes, replace final release acceptance, or gate ordinary semantic development. Foundation requirement gravity/bootstrap-equivalence-before-retirement: Before retiring a named seed component, compare the declared predecessor and Gravity successor stages on accepted and rejected programs, canonical outputs and diagnostics; record residual TCB and an explicit retirement decision for that component only. Refusals: Deny retirement for missing stage products, unreviewed drift, stale compiler/source identities or required conformance failures; an intermediate stage admission cannot retire unrelated seed components. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix - Locked source/compiler/provider/target build graph and canonical rebuild comparison. Foundation requirement gravity/bootstrap-staged-trust-reduction: Record each actual compiler/platform component migration into Gravity with source and predecessor/successor compiler identities, reproducible stage products, exact supported subset and the measured residual seed/TCB inventory. Refusals: Reject a claimed seed reduction without an actual migrated product or with missing lineage; plans, supplied success labels and one migrated helper cannot establish complete seed absence. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix - Locked source/compiler/provider/target build graph and canonical rebuild comparison.\n\n", :id "release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-stage-compatibilityequivalence-across-the-claimed-compiler", :before "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-stage-compatibilityequivalence-across-the-claimed-compiler` Complete stage compatibility/equivalence across the claimed compiler\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Equivalence contract](../../docs/phase-15-bootstrap-and-self-hosting/209-boot7-self-hosting-validation-and-equivalence-plan.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Fresh stage-to-stage outputs and diagnostics, residual trusted-code inventory BOOT1/BOOT3/BOOT5/BOOT7: Publish a versioned row for every claimed stage and authoritative module revision, naming source/compiler/artifact identities, supported and unsupported documents/features/profiles/backends/runtime/package/library/test closure, owned or deferred gaps, conformance links and release eligibility. Record exact compiler-module ownership and residual TCB with measurable migration delta. Compare both named compilers and canonical artifacts under declared applicable hash/manifest/diagnostic/conformance/runtime/IR/performance/accepted-delta modes; preserve stable codes/spans and provenance. Reject missing outputs, implicit inherited support, omitted stage rows, unsupported claims, stale matrix versions and unexplained drift; accept deltas only with policy-linked review. Performance bounds apply only when performance is part of acceptance; no compiler work quota is introduced. Execute the intermediate authoritative stage/module admission decision against this exact candidate and declared subset, consuming the fresh conformance, equivalence/accepted-delta, matrix, provenance, TCB and applicable audit records. Record admit or deny with candidate/source/compiler/artifact identities and failed predicates. Deny failing applicable suites, stale or missing required evidence, unexplained drift, unsupported claimed support and missing ownership/matrix updates. Exercise both a valid intermediate admission and each refusal. Retain explicitly owned/deferred gaps outside the claimed subset; final release policy separately rejects unreviewed gaps for claimed release support. This decision does not produce the evidence it consumes, replace final release acceptance, or gate ordinary semantic development.\n\n", :after-sha256 "3e28f0b311b863f2a55ee0e5fbf2bd4d4ad9add1a0c88893646c9f95ef52aae0"} {:path "specs/runtime-workflow/tasks.md", :requirements ["gravity/explicit-runtime-service-dependencies" "gravity/runtime-manifest-closure"], :before-sha256 "4723a7369dab1473851f2053a601e3f1bc9e6a99cc9591d040603d90612c9325", :marker "runtime-implementation-tasks", :operation :replace-exact-task-record, :status-change :none, :after "- [ ] `runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection` Implement explicit family selection and no-runtime rejection\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Selection validator](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/runtimes/00284-runtime-selection-validate.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Actual service link/load inspection for every claimed profile/target and forbidden-service rejection. R1/R2/R4: explicit family selection and compatible composition; linked/generated/delegated/external/forbidden service records consumed by backend, package, observability, conformance and self-hosting tools; runtime-none entry/reset/interrupt/ABI, sections, memory map, alignment and required target stack evidence; generated checks and panic helpers with provenance. Reject hidden GC, allocator, scheduler, reflection, eval, host IO and hosted-profile leakage; unsupported dynamic forms reject unless eliminated with evidence. Dependencies: Lower supplies target ABI/artifacts, Legality supplies profile facts, and Build supplies package policy; no product ISA or platform choice is made here. Foundation requirement gravity/explicit-runtime-service-dependencies: For every actually used runtime service, emit the selected runtime/provider, service contract/version, effect/grant, profile and source dependency and demonstrate its use across that declared boundary. Refusals: Reject an undeclared allocator, IO, reflection, dynamic dispatch or hosted service, including a transitive service in a no-runtime artifact, before claiming support. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products; lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs - Verified MIR/domain-operation disposition matrix and target/provider/preservation inputs. Foundation requirement gravity/runtime-manifest-closure: Close the selected runtime manifest transitively over actual linked/loaded services and providers, declared effects/grants, profiles and source dependencies; compare manifest declarations with the produced artifact's service usage. Refusals: Reject an undeclared transitive allocator/IO/reflection/dispatch/thread dependency or an unavailable service in a no-runtime profile; a chosen runtime label cannot authorize the missing service. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs - Verified MIR/domain-operation disposition matrix and target/provider/preservation inputs; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products; build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix - Locked source/compiler/provider/target build graph and canonical rebuild comparison.\n\n", :id "runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection", :before "- [ ] `runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection` Implement explicit family selection and no-runtime rejection\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Selection validator](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/runtimes/00284-runtime-selection-validate.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Actual service link/load inspection for every claimed profile/target and forbidden-service rejection. R1/R2/R4: explicit family selection and compatible composition; linked/generated/delegated/external/forbidden service records consumed by backend, package, observability, conformance and self-hosting tools; runtime-none entry/reset/interrupt/ABI, sections, memory map, alignment and required target stack evidence; generated checks and panic helpers with provenance. Reject hidden GC, allocator, scheduler, reflection, eval, host IO and hosted-profile leakage; unsupported dynamic forms reject unless eliminated with evidence. Dependencies: Lower supplies target ABI/artifacts, Legality supplies profile facts, and Build supplies package policy; no product ISA or platform choice is made here.\n\n", :after-sha256 "91dfae87672bd2f2dc244d800bed4eea86cedf909956e1ce6a9970e80a3a06f4"} {:path "specs/runtime-workflow/tasks.md", :requirements ["gravity/interop-boundary-manifest" "gravity/interop-is-not-host-semantics"], :before-sha256 "05ce448769b4861003c327556d05ec017cd65ed92eea560f7158ae49b5ea6375", :marker "runtime-implementation-tasks", :operation :replace-exact-task-record, :status-change :none, :after "- [ ] `runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries` Implement memory, concurrency and typed FFI boundaries\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Runtime contracts](../../docs/phase-08-runtime-architecture/README.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Allocation, lifetime, transfer, race and foreign-failure conformance with explicit providers. Execute the [SAFE2-SAFE8 contracts](../../docs/phase-02-safety/README.md): declared allocation and cleanup failures, partial initialization cleanup, region/arena generation and borrow checks, release through the correct allocator/provider, callback lifetime/thread/reentrancy/release and foreign error/exception/promise translation. Reject retained borrows, post-reset access, missing FFI declarations, unsupported atomics and unsynchronized mutable access; validate immutable sharing, lock cleanup, actor/channel transfer and declared backpressure/cancellation. Inspect actual checks and audit records, with no hidden GC or host-thread fallback. . R3/R5/R6/R10: allocation/deallocation/provider manifests, no-allocation and region/arena escape rejection, linear acquire/transfer/consume ledgers, device address-space/transfer/synchronization/lifetime checks, audited raw-memory wrappers, and agreement of retained checks with exact proof-elision records; atomics with target memory order/scope/alignment, structured task parent or explicit lifecycle owner, cancellation cleanup and failure propagation, actor/channel schemas with ordering/backpressure/transfer policy; FFI symbol/loading policy, ABI/layout conformance, null/handle/lifetime/ownership/error adapters and callbacks re-entering capability/taint/thread-affinity/scheduler checks. Reject mismatched providers, races, orphan tasks, unsupported atomics, schemaless messages, raw extern safe calls and invalid callback entry. Dependencies: ownership and Legality supply compile-time facts, Lower supplies target layouts, Auth supplies grants, and distributed execution supplies replay policy; runtime debug checks cannot substitute for compile-time safety. P4/P5: host-object/native FFI records bind runtime/version/symbol, Gravity and foreign types, rooting/ownership/lifetime, nullability, failure mapping, affinity, ABI, effects/grants and safe wrappers. Insufficient host metadata permits opaque provider-only handles, not unrestricted manipulation; raw native imports are not directly safe-callable. Exercise positive boundaries and missing metadata, ungranted call, invalid lifetime and untranslated failure rejection. Foundation requirement gravity/interop-boundary-manifest: Produce and consume the typed foreign boundary manifest with applicable ABI/layout, ownership/transfer/lifetime, null/error/callback/thread, host/schema/provider, effects/grants and provenance obligations; demonstrate a conforming boundary invocation. Refusals: Reject a missing applicable obligation, incompatible ABI/schema/provider, invalid ownership transfer or absent authority; a declaration-only check does not prove actual conversion or callback execution. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): schema - Versioned source schema, generated validators/codecs and parity artifacts; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products. Foundation requirement gravity/interop-is-not-host-semantics: Normalize an admitted foreign value/failure/callback through its declared typed and audited Gravity boundary while preserving Gravity errors, source identity, effects and capability requirements. Refusals: Reject a host null, exception, reflection/loading convention or object-identity assumption leaking into portable Gravity semantics; keep actual adaptation separate from manifest publication. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products; diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/integrate-runtimebuildeditor-consumers-without-rule-drift - Actual runtime/compiler/tool structured diagnostics with stable owning codes and provenance.\n\n", :id "runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries", :before "- [ ] `runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries` Implement memory, concurrency and typed FFI boundaries\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Runtime contracts](../../docs/phase-08-runtime-architecture/README.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Allocation, lifetime, transfer, race and foreign-failure conformance with explicit providers. Execute the [SAFE2-SAFE8 contracts](../../docs/phase-02-safety/README.md): declared allocation and cleanup failures, partial initialization cleanup, region/arena generation and borrow checks, release through the correct allocator/provider, callback lifetime/thread/reentrancy/release and foreign error/exception/promise translation. Reject retained borrows, post-reset access, missing FFI declarations, unsupported atomics and unsynchronized mutable access; validate immutable sharing, lock cleanup, actor/channel transfer and declared backpressure/cancellation. Inspect actual checks and audit records, with no hidden GC or host-thread fallback. . R3/R5/R6/R10: allocation/deallocation/provider manifests, no-allocation and region/arena escape rejection, linear acquire/transfer/consume ledgers, device address-space/transfer/synchronization/lifetime checks, audited raw-memory wrappers, and agreement of retained checks with exact proof-elision records; atomics with target memory order/scope/alignment, structured task parent or explicit lifecycle owner, cancellation cleanup and failure propagation, actor/channel schemas with ordering/backpressure/transfer policy; FFI symbol/loading policy, ABI/layout conformance, null/handle/lifetime/ownership/error adapters and callbacks re-entering capability/taint/thread-affinity/scheduler checks. Reject mismatched providers, races, orphan tasks, unsupported atomics, schemaless messages, raw extern safe calls and invalid callback entry. Dependencies: ownership and Legality supply compile-time facts, Lower supplies target layouts, Auth supplies grants, and distributed execution supplies replay policy; runtime debug checks cannot substitute for compile-time safety. P4/P5: host-object/native FFI records bind runtime/version/symbol, Gravity and foreign types, rooting/ownership/lifetime, nullability, failure mapping, affinity, ABI, effects/grants and safe wrappers. Insufficient host metadata permits opaque provider-only handles, not unrestricted manipulation; raw native imports are not directly safe-callable. Exercise positive boundaries and missing metadata, ungranted call, invalid lifetime and untranslated failure rejection.\n\n", :after-sha256 "4e47a02b8265746a3423dddde06a8147d8a293945891fdce2e038ff1fdbdb3ee"} {:path "specs/tools-workflow/tasks.md", :requirements ["gravity/tooling-semantic-consistency"], :before-sha256 "2b3e5859f3974dd80510f259ebbb3ea7a56c824f21d289e61c34b39cee65cc19", :marker "tools-implementation-tasks", :operation :replace-exact-task-record, :status-change :none, :after "- [ ] `tools/finite-service-outcomes-and-remaining-work/ir-explorer-compiler-tool-maintainer` IR Explorer / compiler-tool maintainer\n\nStatus: Open\n\nRemaining implementation tasks: Expose actual stage artifacts and source edges; implement semantic-versus-format diff; show failed pass and preservation/proof records\n\nClosing evidence and governing contract: Version/profile/target and artifact IDs present? Missing/stale stages shown honestly? Check-elision evidence visible? [IR inspector](../../docs/phase-13-tooling-and-developer-experience/186-t10-compiler-explorer-and-ir-inspector-design.md) Verify every T10 stage with compiler/project/profile/target/stage identity, available semantic facts, upstream/source/generated-origin edges, pass input/output and target assumptions. Export IR JSON, diff/preservation/source-map/redacted bundles; reject missing context, lost origins, secret exports and check removal without preservation evidence. Foundation requirement gravity/tooling-semantic-consistency: Make formatter/LSP/REPL/inspection consumers use actual compiler diagnostics, syntax/source identities and compiled profile/effect/capability boundaries; compare supported tool and ordinary compiler results on the same accepted and rejected inputs. Refusals: Reject stale tool diagnostics, lost syntax identity, a refactor changing source meaning or interactive evaluation bypassing compiled grant/profile checks; no alternate tool-only language semantics. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/integrate-runtimebuildeditor-consumers-without-rule-drift - Actual runtime/compiler/tool structured diagnostics with stable owning codes and provenance; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products.\n\n", :id "tools/finite-service-outcomes-and-remaining-work/ir-explorer-compiler-tool-maintainer", :before "- [ ] `tools/finite-service-outcomes-and-remaining-work/ir-explorer-compiler-tool-maintainer` IR Explorer / compiler-tool maintainer\n\nStatus: Open\n\nRemaining implementation tasks: Expose actual stage artifacts and source edges; implement semantic-versus-format diff; show failed pass and preservation/proof records\n\nClosing evidence and governing contract: Version/profile/target and artifact IDs present? Missing/stale stages shown honestly? Check-elision evidence visible? [IR inspector](../../docs/phase-13-tooling-and-developer-experience/186-t10-compiler-explorer-and-ir-inspector-design.md) Verify every T10 stage with compiler/project/profile/target/stage identity, available semantic facts, upstream/source/generated-origin edges, pass input/output and target assumptions. Export IR JSON, diff/preservation/source-map/redacted bundles; reject missing context, lost origins, secret exports and check removal without preservation evidence.\n\n", :after-sha256 "5243ed3ab96fe2ffb5016c608532080056689d60b9badc19f88a847b78e5984e"} {:path "specs/tools-workflow/tasks.md", :requirements ["gravity/canonical-concept-vocabulary" "gravity/cross-phase-term-change-control" "gravity/domain-concept-layer-map" "gravity/qualify-ambiguous-normative-terms"], :before-sha256 "d4e34692fc3d908e5f372cc3d5f7cd7058c75b1daf8a7761802b0cdf77581858", :marker "tools-implementation-tasks", :operation :replace-exact-task-record, :status-change :none, :after "- [ ] `tools/finite-service-outcomes-and-remaining-work/lint-analysis-tool-maintainer` Lint / analysis-tool maintainer\n\nStatus: Open\n\nRemaining implementation tasks: Implement the contract rule classes against named compiler/manifest facts; add project-scoped baselines and rule explanations; implement checked fixes and structured export\n\nClosing evidence and governing contract: Rule source/facts and applicability visible? Unsafe fixes rejected? Baseline/fail-on-new reproducible? [Linter](../../docs/phase-13-tooling-and-developer-experience/180-t4-linter-specification.md) Require rule id/severity/inputs/fixability/profile/target and source/manifest spans; cover every T4 rule class, JSON/SARIF, baseline and rule-coverage artifacts, stable explain-rule output and combined source/manifest analysis. Reject unknown rules, unavailable facts, policy-forbidden stale spans, unchecked fixes and policy-blocking release findings. Foundation requirement gravity/canonical-concept-vocabulary: Publish the D3 reference meanings and relationships for profile, target, backend, runtime, effect, capability, safety outcome, artifact and file, and check representative compiler/package/runtime manifests against those meanings. Refusals: Reject a manifest that equates an effect with authority, a profile with a backend, or an artifact with its storage file; retain the offending span/field and owning concept reference. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Foundation requirement gravity/cross-phase-term-change-control: Before downstream reliance on a changed cross-phase concept, update the canonical D3 definition and affected contract/schema references together, record the compatibility decision and invalidate dependent terminology checks. Refusals: Reject use of a changed downstream meaning with an unchanged canonical definition, stale dependent checks or an unrecorded compatibility impact. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-each-claimed-component-to-exact-implementation-and-conformance - Exact component/slice contracts, declared unsupported scope and claimed-support evidence. Foundation requirement gravity/domain-concept-layer-map: Publish a domain-concept map relating each declared concept to its source forms, Core/domain IR boundary, emitted artifact, effects and required capabilities; verify a representative domain product against that map. Refusals: Reject an unmapped claimed concept, a host API substituted for its source meaning or a mapping that treats an effect declaration as a capability grant. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products. Foundation requirement gravity/qualify-ambiguous-normative-terms: For normative uses whose meaning affects implementation, require an explicit qualified D3 concept or owning contract reference; report the exact ambiguous span and the competing interpretations. Refusals: Reject unqualified uses such as runtime/profile/target or effect/capability where they change the required implementation meaning; ordinary nonnormative prose does not create a new terminology gate. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion.\n\n", :id "tools/finite-service-outcomes-and-remaining-work/lint-analysis-tool-maintainer", :before "- [ ] `tools/finite-service-outcomes-and-remaining-work/lint-analysis-tool-maintainer` Lint / analysis-tool maintainer\n\nStatus: Open\n\nRemaining implementation tasks: Implement the contract rule classes against named compiler/manifest facts; add project-scoped baselines and rule explanations; implement checked fixes and structured export\n\nClosing evidence and governing contract: Rule source/facts and applicability visible? Unsafe fixes rejected? Baseline/fail-on-new reproducible? [Linter](../../docs/phase-13-tooling-and-developer-experience/180-t4-linter-specification.md) Require rule id/severity/inputs/fixability/profile/target and source/manifest spans; cover every T4 rule class, JSON/SARIF, baseline and rule-coverage artifacts, stable explain-rule output and combined source/manifest analysis. Reject unknown rules, unavailable facts, policy-forbidden stale spans, unchecked fixes and policy-blocking release findings.\n\n", :after-sha256 "674d0ac69e8f40862074e32eed3f2457ac9cb1e02a0d814e498ca1316c06ab9c"}], :unresolved-mapping-ids [], :unresolved-semantic-decision-ids ["gravity/canonical-pass-order"], :kind :guarded-foundation-historical-gap-completion-proposal, :completed-mapping-proposals 52, :operations [{:collection :residual-records, :id "gravity/ai-tool-schema-policy-record", :operation :propose-existing-task-criterion, :before {:primary-source-contract "D0", :source-facet-ids ["facet/foundation/329073b00bd2e93539eb8049" "facet/foundation/d5f96af8cb61ea30de96513f" "facet/foundation/b74d7eff555494fdc4b548e6" "facet/foundation/1527c7187938c435bc76174d" "facet/foundation/1f7b39294d5e2e3f57b10845" "facet/foundation/5dc7a345187130e3e60e9de1" "facet/foundation/ae564e9b496c99db8b8b6a48" "facet/foundation/7c31fb504bea9e1199dd5451" "facet/foundation/557f36f6329baa78ba7c6a72" "facet/foundation/0964b041922655167e1ed203" "facet/foundation/e0969b04780a15f9c3d2dac4" "facet/foundation/4d101049b1e75abe93fb6884" "facet/foundation/ec5169a3f4078e2c6a697ddf" "facet/foun